what does elektra bring to the table  that captain america can't is victor von  doom really a better villain than ultron  we love the mcu we're not knocking it  one bit but the old marvel movies just  did some things better  there isn't a superhero film out there  at least on the marvel side of things  that tells a more compelling and  accurate origin story than the original  spider-man not only does it carry the  heart of the original marvel comic books  on its sleeve it combines the origin  directly with one of spidey's most  formidable foes likewise the 2005  fantastic four film angley's hulk and  the punisher among others set their  title characters up for success early on  how is this done by establishing a clear  origin story that often directly ties  our heroes to their most iconic villains  while mcu films like iron man and  captain america the first avenger stand  out as solid origin stories most mcu  films skip their inception completely  instead the films usually dive right  into the action to keep their audience's  attention that or characters are  introduced in another film before  getting their own standalone which also  often skip the origin stories this can  be a huge disservice to both the  characters and the audience peter parker  watching his uncle ben die bruce  banner's childhood flashbacks and  logan's frustrated attempts to uncover  his own story are what grounds and  guides the heroes plus who doesn't love  watching the fantastic four as they get  hit with cosmic rays from space he rise  and shine big boy how you feeling  there's no doubt that one of the things  we love the most about movies like  guardians of the galaxy and thor  ragnarok is the humor the blend of  character growth with self-deprecating  jokes is a true blue staple of the mcu  and for good reason it works i usually  spin it really fast and it would it  would pull me off oh my god emma put you  off the ground in fact many of us  rewatched these films over again just  for the laughs but the old marvel films  took a different approach while there  are clear moments of levity and x-men  spider-man and daredevil the films don't  allow the humor to hold them back from  telling more refined stories raymie's  spider-man trilogy is the perfect  example of blending spidey's humor with  compelling stories that feel honest raw  and genuinely human  i will  always be spider-man the x-men series  developed hugh jackman's wolverine in  ways that no mcu character has simply by  taking the character and his mythos  seriously rather than making a joke out  of them the only reason an incredible  film like logan could have even been  made is because of the groundwork they'd  laid with the character years prior  there's a lot to be said about a complex  interconnected universe where howard the  duck can chill with an immortal elder  and 20 years worth of peter parker's can  meet up to make meta jokes about their  various movies faults it's a whole lot  of fun for fans but it also means you  have to keep up with dozens of releases  to understand everything that's going on  one thing the old marvel movies really  had going for them was that they were  truly stand alone you didn't have to  watch ghostwriter to understand a scene  or two in x-men the last stand and  that's something of a lost art nowadays  we've all gotten so used to  interconnected stories and universes  that we expect them now at every turn  aside from the x-men and blade films  which really build off each previous  installment most of the old marvel  flicks can be consumed on their own  spider-man 2 is just as great if you  haven't seen the first film as it is if  you have and even elektra isn't  completely bound by the daredevil film  she first appeared in if captain america  civil war proved anything it's that  sometimes being too interconnected can  hurt the growth of your primary  characters and that's not something the  old marvel films had to worry about  rather each made sure to focus on their  own localized story before expanding the  world around them  since the foundation of the mcu the  franchise has struggled primarily with  their villains aside from loki thanos  killmonger vulture and one or two  baddies from the netflix shows many mcu  villains aren't terribly compelling  interesting or even believable most of  them don't stand out as anything other  than pale imitations of their heroes and  not in a good way the old marvel films  however understood their villains  completely our heroes main foes were  dark murky reflections of themselves and  not just because they had a similar  stark tech suit of armor rather they  made similar choices to our heroes but  with different results often warping  their own perspective of truth and  justice to fit their own agendas the  dichotomy between characters like  spider-man and green goblin professor x  and magneto and reed richards and victor  von doom is fascinating powerful and  full of surprises  in fact some of these villains are so  iconic that they even brought a bunch of  them back for spider-man no way home  atta boy  the old marvel movies also dealt with a  completely different set of  philosophical implications than most in  the mcu while iron man focuses heavily  on war on terror politics and the  captain america films reference patriot  act surveillance earlier marvel pictures  went for more universal down to earth  themes they dove into sociology  philosophy and even religion like the  original marvel comics before them the  x-men trilogy ran underlying themes of  equality hoping to remind us that people  should be treated the same whether they  have a difference in appearance or  ability this was ultimately the message  that stan lee hoped to convey with their  famed mutant characters and the fox  films handled it pretty well the  spider-man trilogy heavily promotes  moral notions of responsibility which  stand out among all superhero films as  being some of the most powerful ideas  explored in the genre the daredevil film  even touches on matt murdock's  catholicism and how his role as hell's  kitchen's guardian devil is heavily  influenced by his faith ghost rider  explores the moral and spiritual  implications of selling one's soul  likewise fantastic four much like the  mcu's guardians of the galaxy now  promotes the idea that you can find your  true family through friendships they  weren't always the best films but  there's no denying that the old marvel  films had a depth to them that has yet  to be fully replicated  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite marvel movies are coming  soon subscribe to our youtube channel  and hit the bell so you don't miss a  single one  [Music]  you
 

